---
description: Pearl Luxe theme rules for Teams for Linux
globs: app/assets/css/pearlLuxe.css, app/assets/css/pearlLuxeNight.css, app/customCSS/**, app/profileDialogs/**, app/joinMeetingDialog/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Colours, radii, shadows and fonts come only from --lx-* tokens (tokens/pearl-luxe.tokens.css). Never introduce new hex values.
- Gold (--lx-gold) is decorative only; text accents use --lx-gold-ink.
- Light and Night share every rule; differences live only in token values. Primary fills use --lx-primary with --lx-on-primary text, never --lx-espresso directly.
- Serif display font only for page and conversation titles.
- Theme CSS may change colour, type, radius, shadow and spacing; never display:none, position or width changes on Teams controls.
- Prefer data-tid, role and aria-* selectors over generated class names.
- Do not modify CSP, IPC, contextIsolation, sandbox, nodeIntegration, startup flags or capture consent.
- Every text colour must pass WCAG AA on its background; keep :focus-visible rings.
